  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/happymimimix/RePhiEdit-Modded/zipball/1.3.0+1.2.1+2.4.0",
  "body": "Bundled a chart mover made by myself\r\n\r\nUsage: \r\nOpen chart mover from start menu\r\nSelect a chart in the file open dialog\r\nInput move amount (Decimal value allowed)\r\nDone! \r\nChart will be saved to ****-Moved.json\r\n\r\nRe:Phiedit gets very slow when drawing curved notes with density more than 1024. \r\nSo this tool could be very useful at creating very dense notes in crazy impossible charts. \r\nMake a time move of 0.00048828125, which is 1/2048. \r\nThen merge the moved chart to obtain notes with 1/2048 density. \r\nDo the above operation once more with move amount 0.000244140625, which is 1/4096. \r\nYou can obtain notes with density of 1/4096! \r\n\r\nAlso, for people who like to make a marathon containing hundreds of different charts. \r\nThis tool can save a large amount of work for you. \r\nCheck first how many bars the previous song has and move the second chart by that amount. \r\nAfter you've moved all charts with this tool, merge everything with the chart merger tool I created before. \r\nMerge the audio with Fl Studio or any other audio editors you like and your marathon is done! \r\n",
